{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"assignments\":[{\"assignment_status\":\"PROPOSED\",\"candidate_id\":\"node.00787ab10a284a072204b281\",\"question\":{\"actor\":\"The covered UCITS fund seeking relief from the SFC’s prior-approval requirement.\",\"control_id\":\"relief_eligibility_1\",\"false_means\":\"Within scope, this test does not establish relief. It does not establish an approval duty, prohibition or non-compliance. Outside scope no determination is supplied; unknown inputs remain unknown.\",\"question\":\"Does the selected material post-authorisation investment change qualify for item (ii)’s removal of SFC prior approval, including the proposed exclusion for a preserved legacy application?\",\"result_kind\":\"REQUIREMENT_SATISFIED\",\"source_evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u5.840\"},{\"quote\":\"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696\"},{\"quote\":\"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809\"}],\"temporal_basis\":\"Assessment on or after 28 November 2025 is a result condition. An application received before that date and still without approval or authorisation at that date blocks relief under the proposed interpretation. Selection of the legally relevant assessment event remains unresolved.\",\"true_means\":\"Within scope, the commencement condition is met, the change complies with home requirements, involves neither novel nor complex product features, has no possible local policy implications, and has no preserved legacy application. This establishes only the proposed relief conditions, not overall compliance or satisfaction of notification, filing or post-vetting duties.\",\"unit_of_assessment\":\"One material post-authorisation change to an investment objective, policy or restriction of a UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, or a UK-domiciled scheme authorised as UK UCITS, together with the selected application history.\"}},{\"assignment_status\":\"PROPOSED\",\"candidate_id\":\"node.074087c89e3a3304960f612e\",\"question\":{\"actor\":\"The covered UCITS fund seeking relief from the SFC’s prior-approval requirement.\",\"control_id\":\"relief_eligibility_2\",\"false_means\":\"Within scope, the proposed removal is unavailable; this does not independently establish an approval obligation or non-compliance. Outside scope no determination is supplied; unknown inputs remain unknown.\",\"question\":\"Does the selected material post-authorisation investment change satisfy the substantive, commencement and pending-application conditions for removal of SFC prior approval under the proposed transition reading?\",\"result_kind\":\"REQUIREMENT_SATISFIED\",\"source_evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u5.840\"},{\"quote\":\"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696\"},{\"quote\":\"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809\"}],\"temporal_basis\":\"The assessment date must be on or after 28 November 2025. An application received before that date with neither approval nor authorisation granted by that date is treated as an exclusion from relief.\",\"true_means\":\"Within scope, home requirements are met, none of novelty, complexity or possible local policy implications applies, commencement has occurred, and no pending pre-effective application excludes relief. Continuing notification and post-vetting duties are not assessed.\",\"unit_of_assessment\":\"One material change to an investment objective, policy or restriction in a post-authorisation matter for a UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, or a UK-domiciled scheme authorised as UK UCITS, including its application history.\"}},{\"assignment_status\":\"PROPOSED\",\"candidate_id\":\"node.1bf6918f69c6b37738daeb83\",\"question\":{\"actor\":\"The fund within the circular’s defined UCITS class seeking removal of SFC prior approval.\",\"control_id\":\"defined_scope_relief_eligibility\",\"false_means\":\"Within scope, this removal is unavailable under the proposed reading; approval is not thereby necessarily required and non-compliance is not established. A fund or change outside scope receives no determination. Unknown facts remain unknown.\",\"question\":\"Within the circular’s defined UCITS and material post-authorisation investment-change scope, does the identified change qualify for item (ii)’s removal of prior SFC approval under the proposed commencement and transition assumptions?\",\"result_kind\":\"REQUIREMENT_SATISFIED\",\"source_evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"For this circular, UCITS funds means (i) Undertakings for Collective Investment in Transferable Securities (UCITS) domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland and the Netherlands, and (ii) collective investment schemes domiciled in the United Kingdom authorised as UK UCITS.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556\"},{\"quote\":\"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u5.840\"},{\"quote\":\"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809\"},{\"quote\":\"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696\"}],\"temporal_basis\":\"On or after 28 November 2025 is a result condition. Application receipt before that date and absence of approval or authorisation at that date jointly establish the proposed legacy exclusion.\",\"true_means\":\"The in-scope change meets home requirements, involves no novel or complex product features or possible local policy implications, satisfies commencement, and has no preserved pre-effective pending application. No separate home-supervision condition is imposed. Notification, filing, post-vetting and overall compliance are not decided.\",\"unit_of_assessment\":\"One identified material post-authorisation change to an investment objective, policy or restriction, assessed as a whole, for a fund meeting the quoted circular-specific UCITS definition, together with its application history.\"}},{\"assignment_status\":\"PROPOSED\",\"candidate_id\":\"node.4d548f2e09bc36ef51212f64\",\"question\":{\"actor\":\"The covered UCITS fund seeking removal of SFC prior approval outside the legacy-application transition.\",\"control_id\":\"nonlegacy_relief_eligibility\",\"false_means\":\"Within scope, home compliance or absence of an exception fails, so this removal is unavailable. This does not establish a prohibition, non-compliance or the complete underlying approval obligation. Pre-effective assessments and legacy pending applications are outside scope, not false results. Unknown facts remain unknown.\",\"question\":\"For a covered material post-authorisation investment change assessed after commencement and outside the legacy-application transition, are the home-compliance and exception conditions for removal of prior SFC approval satisfied?\",\"result_kind\":\"REQUIREMENT_SATISFIED\",\"source_evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u5.840\"},{\"quote\":\"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696\"},{\"quote\":\"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809\"}],\"temporal_basis\":\"Scope requires an assessment date on or after 28 November 2025 and excludes applications received before that date that remained without approval or authorisation at that date. The assessment date does not establish a universal implementation-date test.\",\"true_means\":\"Within scope, the change complies with applicable home requirements and involves neither novel nor complex product features nor possible local policy implications. It therefore meets the stated removal conditions, without determining overall compliance.\",\"unit_of_assessment\":\"One material post-authorisation investment-objective, policy or restriction change for a UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, or a UK-domiciled scheme authorised as UK UCITS, outside the specified legacy transition.\"}},{\"assignment_status\":\"PROPOSED\",\"candidate_id\":\"node.4e6a162c35678e9ddf17ad8e\",\"question\":{\"actor\":\"The covered SFC-authorised UCITS fund seeking removal of prior SFC approval.\",\"control_id\":\"change_and_application_relief_eligibility\",\"false_means\":\"Within scope, removal is unavailable under this model because a substantive condition or the application-history condition fails. This does not establish prohibition or an independent approval obligation. Outside scope no conclusion is supplied; unknown inputs remain unknown.\",\"question\":\"For the identified covered material post-authorisation investment change assessed on or after commencement, are the substantive relief conditions met and is there no pending pre-effective application barring reliance under the proposed transition interpretation?\",\"result_kind\":\"REQUIREMENT_SATISFIED\",\"source_evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u5.840\"},{\"quote\":\"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809\"},{\"quote\":\"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696\"}],\"temporal_basis\":\"Scope requires assessment for proposed implementation on or after 28 November 2025. The result excludes a related application received before that date with neither approval nor authorisation granted at the transition.\",\"true_means\":\"The change satisfies every applicable home requirement, no involved feature is novel or complex, the change has no possible local policy implications, and no pending pre-effective application defeats relief under the proposed reading. This confers no legal approval and does not determine post-vetting compliance.\",\"unit_of_assessment\":\"One identified material change affecting at least one investment objective, policy or restriction of an SFC-authorised fund, including all involved features and related applications; the fund must be a UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, or a UK-domiciled scheme authorised as UK UCITS.\"}},{\"assignment_status\":\"UNCERTAIN\",\"candidate_id\":\"node.8eb374ffa546ddd2ba291e37\",\"question\":{\"actor\":\"The covered UCITS fund or applicant seeking actual relief from SFC prior approval while its existing application remains subject to processing.\",\"control_id\":\"actual_relief_with_preserved_processing\",\"false_means\":\"A resolved false answer would mean actual item (ii) relief is unavailable for the selected change and application, without independently establishing an approval duty or non-compliance. The candidate supplies no executable false condition: preserved processing alone is not treated as proof of substantive disqualification. Unknown or unresolved availability must not be converted to false.\",\"question\":\"Is item (ii)’s removal of prior SFC approval actually available for the selected change and application when substantive qualification is assessed separately from preservation of the existing application process?\",\"result_kind\":\"REQUIREMENT_SATISFIED\",\"source_evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u5.840\"},{\"quote\":\"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809\"},{\"quote\":\"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696\"}],\"temporal_basis\":\"Retains commencement on 28 November 2025 and the distinction between applications received before that date and still unapproved or unauthorised at transition. The effect of preserved processing on actual relief remains unresolved.\",\"true_means\":\"A resolved true answer would establish actual availability of relief, not merely satisfaction of home-compliance and exception tests. The candidate does not supply a complete rule connecting substantive qualification and preserved processing, so substantive qualification alone cannot produce this true answer.\",\"unit_of_assessment\":\"One material post-authorisation investment-objective, policy or restriction change of a UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, or a UK-domiciled scheme authorised as UK UCITS, together with its selected existing application. Substantive change qualification and application processing are distinct questions within this unresolved assessment.\"}},{\"assignment_status\":\"PROPOSED\",\"candidate_id\":\"node.b66b3e831bb98a12db59dffa\",\"question\":{\"actor\":\"The covered SFC-authorised UCITS fund whose change is assessed against item (ii)’s substantive conditions.\",\"control_id\":\"substantive_removal_conditions\",\"false_means\":\"Within scope, at least one substantive home-requirements or exception test fails. This does not establish whether prior approval is legally required. Outside scope no conclusion is supplied; unknown inputs remain unknown.\",\"question\":\"Does the identified material post-authorisation investment change satisfy item (ii)’s substantive home-requirements and exception tests, independently of the treatment of any existing application?\",\"result_kind\":\"REQUIREMENT_SATISFIED\",\"source_evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u5.840\"},{\"quote\":\"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809\"},{\"quote\":\"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696\"}],\"temporal_basis\":\"Scope requires assessment on or after 28 November 2025. Application history, including pending status at commencement and subsequent decisions, is outside this substantive predicate.\",\"true_means\":\"The change meets every applicable home requirement, involves no novel or complex product feature, and has no possible local policy implications. This does not determine actual procedural availability of relief, permission to bypass the existing process, legal approval or overall compliance.\",\"unit_of_assessment\":\"One identified material post-authorisation change affecting at least one investment objective, policy or restriction, including all involved product features without inferred severability, of an SFC-authorised UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, or a UK-domiciled scheme authorised as UK UCITS.\"}},{\"assignment_status\":\"PROPOSED\",\"candidate_id\":\"node.ce439b1cf9ed8301fbb68f94\",\"question\":{\"actor\":\"The covered SFC-authorised UCITS fund seeking removal of the SFC prior-approval requirement.\",\"control_id\":\"dated_relief_eligibility\",\"false_means\":\"Within scope, at least one removal condition fails, including commencement or the proposed application-transition exclusion. This does not by itself establish that prior approval is required. Outside scope no determination is supplied; unknown facts remain unknown.\",\"question\":\"Does the identified material post-authorisation investment change qualify for removal of prior SFC approval on the assessment date, taking account of home requirements, every involved product feature, possible local policy implications and the application transition?\",\"result_kind\":\"REQUIREMENT_SATISFIED\",\"source_evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u5.840\"},{\"quote\":\"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696\"},{\"quote\":\"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809\"}],\"temporal_basis\":\"Assessment on or after 28 November 2025 is a result condition. A covering application received before that date with neither approval nor authorisation granted at that date defeats relief under the proposed reading.\",\"true_means\":\"Within scope, commencement has occurred, home requirements are met, no involved feature is novel or complex, no possible local policy implications exist, and there is no preserved pending pre-effective application. This is relief eligibility, not legal approval, post-vetting performance or overall compliance.\",\"unit_of_assessment\":\"One identified material post-authorisation change to at least one investment objective, policy or restriction, including all involved features and covering application history, of an SFC-authorised UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, or a UK-domiciled scheme authorised as UK UCITS.\"}},{\"assignment_status\":\"PROPOSED\",\"candidate_id\":\"node.ea4d19630f8cab09065b1909\",\"question\":{\"actor\":\"The covered UCITS fund or applicant seeking item (ii) relief from prior SFC approval.\",\"control_id\":\"relief_with_legacy_exclusion\",\"false_means\":\"Within scope, this test does not establish relief. It does not establish an approval duty or non-compliance. Outside scope no determination is supplied; unknown facts remain unknown.\",\"question\":\"Does the identified material post-authorisation investment change qualify for item (ii)’s prior-approval relief when preservation of a legacy application’s existing process is treated as an exclusion from that relief?\",\"result_kind\":\"REQUIREMENT_SATISFIED\",\"source_evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u5.840\"},{\"quote\":\"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809\"},{\"quote\":\"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696\"}],\"temporal_basis\":\"Assessment on or after 28 November 2025 is a result condition; the legally relevant assessment event remains subject to clarification. An application received before that date and still without approval or authorisation at that date blocks relief for the selected application under the proposed inference.\",\"true_means\":\"Within scope, the change satisfies home requirements and commencement, involves no novel or complex product features or possible local policy implications, and has no preserved legacy application. No separate home-supervision test is added. Notification and post-vetting remain distinct.\",\"unit_of_assessment\":\"One identified material post-authorisation investment-objective, policy or restriction change, assessed as a whole with its selected application history, for a UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, or a UK-domiciled scheme authorised as UK UCITS. No severability, withdrawal or resubmission rule is inferred.\"}}]}"}}
